  "summary": "Causal effect identifiability in causal abstractions: A strict hierarchy of criteria and Counterfactual Graph Neural Process (CFGNP) for answering counterfactual queries directly from observational data.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Identifying causal effects from observational data typically requires a fully specified causal graph, an assumption that is often unrealistic in complex or high-dimensional settings.",
